Corrected message:

Keep the view centered on menu, keyboard and typed zoom

Zooming from the menu, a keyboard shortcut or the typed zoom box
anchors on the center of the view, but the rule that keeps an
on-screen image edge from being pushed out of view also applied there
and could pull a centered image to its top-left corner. That rule now
applies only to zooming around the mouse pointer; center zoom keeps
the centered image point centered.

Adds a test for the center case.
